        <p>WASLEY GUILD.—Last Monday a social in cm tion with the above Guild was held in the Wesley Schools. During the earlier part of the evening musical programme was gone through, the followil artistes taking part :—Mr. Hugh Mellor. who perform! pianoforte solos ; Dr. Bennett, violin solo ; Mason, Mrs. Dutton, Dr. Bennett, who also sang. the executants were encored.—During the intei refreshments were handed ronnd by lady meml attached to the Guild.—Afterwards there was a B 1 Bee Competition, and Mr. G. S. IPendlebury being t winner was awarded a prize. There was also on vi; in the room photographs &amp;c., of places and scenes wh.) the late Rev. John Wesley had visited during his 11, time.</p>
