      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-04_WidnesExaminer_art0185" n="art0185">
        <head>Mr. S. M. Crosfleld's Will.</head>
        <p>Mr. S. M. Crosfleld's Will.</p>
        <p>Mr. Sydney Morland Crosfield, Hear/811, and formerly of Morland House, Lymm, who died at the Hotel Metropole, Las Palmas, on January 30th, left estate of the value of £16,490, the peraonalty being nil. Deceased was the son of the late Ir. Morland Crosfield, of Lymm, and a grandson of the late Mr. Joseph Crosfield, the founder of the firm of Messrs. Joseph Crosfield and Sons, Limited. He wag captain of the Warrington Cricket Club for many years, and was also an enthusiastic and prominent member of the Lancashire cricket team, of which on several occasions he acted as captain, and was generally recognized as a ' good all-round sportsman. The testator left to his wife, Mrs. Catherine Gertrude Crosfield, his residence Rynettan, £3OO, the silver tea service presented to him by Sir Frederick and Lady Walker absolutely, and the use for life of his household effects. He left a three-lipped silver cup, won at pigeon shooting, to his cousin Arthur Henry Crosfield, M.P. for Warring- ton, and other shooting prizes and old silver, china, and furniture to his brother, Ernest Morland Crosfield, to whom he also left his guns and fishing tackle. The residue of his property be left to his wife for life, with remainder to his children, whom failing, to hip brother I Ernest for life, and ultimate remainder as to one-half to Mr. Henry flatten Field, and one-half to Thomas Pym Williamson, son of the Rev. T. P. Williamson, of , Thelwall,</p>
      </div>
