      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-04-04_WidnesExaminer_art0218" n="art0218">
        <head>RAILWAY MAN.</head>
        <p>RAILWAY MAN.</p>
        <p>STRONG PRAISE OF DR. MORSE'S INDIAN ROOT PILLS. CONSTIPATION CURED.</p>
        <p>The strong testimony of Mr. T. Payton of 2, Midland Street, Manchester, ought to convince the most sceptical that Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills are a great remedy for this complaint. Mr. T. Payton writes as follows :—" I wish to tell you of the very great benefit I have received from the use of your Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills. I am employed as a gate- man at the Midland Railway Goods depot. For the past two years I have been a sufferer from Constipation, and although I tried a great many medicines none of them seemed to give me any relief. Some time ago a Circular, advertising Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills, was put in my house, and after carefully reading it, I obtained a bottle of the Pills and having given them a fair trial I felt great relief, and I wish to express my gratitude to you for bringing to my notice such a valuable remedy, and shall take great pleasure in recommending the Pills to all my friends.' Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills get at the cause as no other remedy does. They give you clean bowels, a healthy stomach, a lively liver and active kidneys, bracing up the nerves, and toning the whole system. They are a perfect Blood Purifier and a positive and permanent cure for Biliousness, Indigestion, Constipation, Headaches, Sallow Complexion, Liver and Kidney Troubles, Piles, Pimples, Boils and Blotches, and for Female Ailments. For sale by all Chemists and Stores, price Is. I 'id. per bottle, or 6 bottles for 6s. 6d., or will be sent by mail post. paid by the Proprietors, The W. H. Comstock Co., Ltd., 21, Fat eingdon Avenue, London, E.C. I free sample will be sent on receipt of a id. stamp.</p>
      </div>
