        <p>A;pley v. Fairfield Res. or Oughtrington Park Res. Results for March 2Sth. Oughtrin„gton Park 9, Warrington St. Paul's 0. Lymm 7, Latchford 0. Results of Works Competition Matches. Cable Company 3, Nlostyn Tube 1. Locker's 2, Orford Tannery 1. R. A. Naylor 0, Longford Wire 2. Pearson &amp; Knowles (No. 3) 1, " Guardian " Office 1.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON CUP.—FINAL TIE. WARRINGTON ALBIONS v. CASTNER KELLNER. To-day (Saturday) April 4th, on Rylands' Recreation Ground, Gorsey-lane. Kicli-off 3.30. Referee, Mr. Fletcher, Bury.</p>
        <p>Alleged Theft of Piping. At the Warrington Occasional Court on Tuesday before Mr. H. Roberts, William Worslcy, a rag- gatherer, was charged with stealing a quantity of lead piping and brass from the premises of Mr. Edward de Prez, of Moore, on the previous day. P.C. Whalley was on duty at Walton when he met the prisoner and two other youths wheeling a handcart laden with rags. The officer being suspicious examined the contents of the handcart, and found the lead piping and brass. He took Worsley into custody. The case was remanded to the Stockton Heath Petty Sessions.</p>
